WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.617
Start inside the core.

2
00:00:01.617 --> 00:00:06.907
The frontend obtains instructions, and decode identifies the operations.

3
00:00:06.907 --> 00:00:11.904
Issue checks whether operands and execution resources are available.

4
00:00:11.904 --> 00:00:16.533
A scoreboard tracks outstanding instructions and their results.

5
00:00:16.533 --> 00:00:21.603
Execution units then perform arithmetic, branches or memory accesses.

6
00:00:21.603 --> 00:00:30.126
Commit controls when instructions retire and their effects become architectural state, including exception handling.

7
00:00:30.126 --> 00:00:36.886
These boxes describe responsibilities, rather than promising a fixed number of clock cycles.

8
00:00:36.886 --> 00:00:44.234
Outside them, a usable system still needs memory, interconnect, interrupts, debug and boot software.

9
00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:53.860
Keeping that boundary visible helps you decide whether a question belongs in the core configuration or in the surrounding platform.

